WEBVTT

00:46.850 --> 00:48.940
That's my granddaughter!

00:48.940 --> 00:50.400
Attagirl!

00:50.400 --> 00:54.030
But it's too soon for this!

02:33.540 --> 02:34.500
Yuma-chan?

02:35.630 --> 02:36.840
It hurts.

02:37.920 --> 02:41.260
Everyone's staring daggers at me!

02:41.470 --> 02:43.810
Just gotta deal, Toi-san.

02:43.810 --> 02:45.260
What do you expect to happen

02:46.220 --> 02:49.850
when we've got Blondie tailing us?

02:51.230 --> 02:54.820
Hey, do you mind walking a little further back?

02:54.820 --> 02:55.690
Why?

02:55.690 --> 02:56.980
You haven't noticed?

02:56.980 --> 02:57.990
Sumeragi-san?

02:57.990 --> 02:58.490
Yes?

02:59.360 --> 03:01.910
Who's that girl you're with? You know her?

03:01.910 --> 03:03.320
She looks like a foreigner!

03:03.320 --> 03:04.910
Why is she going to school with you?

03:04.910 --> 03:06.410
Is she an exchange student?

03:05.660 --> 03:08.040
Well, uh...

03:08.040 --> 03:11.170
I've got the answers!

03:11.170 --> 03:14.670
This girl's the myth, the legend, the famed Exorc—

03:14.670 --> 03:16.500
Nobody! She's nobody!

03:16.500 --> 03:17.920
What's your name?

03:17.920 --> 03:20.630
Need someone to show you around? I can help.

03:21.590 --> 03:23.010
Let's go while they're distracted.

03:27.390 --> 03:29.180
Don't get in my way.

03:29.180 --> 03:30.810
Yes, Mistress!

03:30.810 --> 03:32.650
Please step on me!

03:32.650 --> 03:36.650
<i>And at that moment, I heard my final chances at an ordinary life</i>

03:36.650 --> 03:40.070
<i>hit the floor and shatter.</i>

03:42.950 --> 03:44.620
A Special Kind of Ordinary!

03:50.540 --> 03:53.370
So she has defeated the Creed Killer.

03:54.080 --> 03:56.090
<i>Clarus Tonitrus...</i>

03:56.090 --> 03:59.840
<i>It seems the decision to let her work independently was the correct one.</i>

04:00.300 --> 04:05.470
You have my gratitude for accepting my unreasonable request.

04:05.470 --> 04:08.890
<i>All according to our Lord's will.</i>

04:08.890 --> 04:09.560
<i>Now then...</i>

04:09.970 --> 04:13.600
<i>May I ask about the other girl?</i>

04:13.600 --> 04:14.400
Of course.

04:14.690 --> 04:16.520
According to Clarus's report,

04:16.520 --> 04:22.570
Sumeragi Matoi obtained a Regalia and called a higher dimensional being down by accident...

04:22.820 --> 04:25.740
<i>...thus achieving Divine Union.</i>

04:26.280 --> 04:28.700
Both the summoning and the Union were,

04:29.100 --> 04:31.660
in all likelihood, unintended.

04:31.660 --> 04:35.370
If I had to guess, external factors were an influence on the matter.

04:35.370 --> 04:36.960
<i>We can't be sure,</i>

04:36.960 --> 04:41.170
<i>but the report implicates that her higher dimensional being is quite strong.</i>

04:41.460 --> 04:45.680
<i>And it only stands to reason that her Regalia must be impressive as well.</i>

04:45.680 --> 04:48.890
<i>We cannot let it fall into the hands of the Nights.</i>

04:49.180 --> 04:52.140
<i>So we shall collect it for ourselves.</i>

04:52.140 --> 04:53.100
But...

04:53.850 --> 04:56.730
Her Regalia is buried deep inside her body,

04:56.730 --> 04:58.480
and has become one with her.

04:58.940 --> 05:02.240
If we were to take it by force, not only would it end her life,

05:02.240 --> 05:04.990
but there is also the possibility that the Regalia would be destroyed.

05:05.360 --> 05:08.070
<i>For the time being, it is in our best interest</i>

05:08.070 --> 05:12.040
<i>to observe and watch over this girl,
and find out what the Nights are planning.</i>

05:13.120 --> 05:14.580
You have my permission.

05:14.580 --> 05:16.750
I'll be expecting a good report.

05:18.580 --> 05:21.590
A higher dimensional being that has countless gods under its command.

05:24.130 --> 05:25.880
Why does Sumeragi Matoi

05:27.130 --> 05:29.420
have that much power?

05:31.930 --> 05:32.810
What do you want?

05:33.600 --> 05:36.520
I hope I'm wrong, but...

05:36.520 --> 05:39.150
Are you really gonna stay there forever?

05:39.150 --> 05:41.150
For as long as I'm ordered to.

05:41.400 --> 05:45.280
How will you eat? Where will you sleep? Do you even have a change of clothes?

05:45.280 --> 05:46.990
That's none of your concern.

05:49.280 --> 05:50.740
Okay, that's it!

05:51.780 --> 05:53.160
Hey! What are you doing?

05:53.160 --> 05:55.200
Just come with me!

05:56.210 --> 05:58.790
The "Secretary Murder" in Suginami?

05:58.790 --> 06:02.000
Yeah, it's unlikely the victim knew their assailant personally.

06:02.460 --> 06:07.300
Look for single men and women who live near the victim.

06:08.590 --> 06:10.220
Right. Do your best.

06:12.180 --> 06:14.180
Sounds like the central office is pretty busy.

06:14.180 --> 06:15.060
I'm back!

06:15.060 --> 06:17.060
Hey Matoi, where did you—

06:17.060 --> 06:19.760
Shingo-san, this girl's staying the night!

06:20.560 --> 06:21.310
Huh?

06:22.110 --> 06:23.980
Uh... okay.

06:23.980 --> 06:26.940
Gimme a few! I'll start dinner soon!

06:28.570 --> 06:30.780
I never knew she had a blonde friend.

06:32.120 --> 06:34.240
So Fatima has involved themselves directly now?

06:34.580 --> 06:38.910
Yes, but that also means Sumeragi Matoi's safety is guaranteed.

06:38.910 --> 06:42.210
If I may, Director, I'd like to investigate further.

06:44.500 --> 06:45.880
Okay!

06:46.260 --> 06:48.470
I'll leave some pajamas and a change of clothes right here.

06:52.350 --> 06:54.930
Why did you invite me into your home?

06:55.220 --> 06:57.600
I couldn't leave you outside like that.

06:57.600 --> 06:59.890
Anybody would do this. It's normal.

06:59.890 --> 07:02.730
Your normal and my normal are different.

07:04.360 --> 07:06.610
I don't think so.

07:07.780 --> 07:09.950
Normal... is just normal.

07:15.160 --> 07:15.950
Huh?

07:17.040 --> 07:17.500
But...

07:18.580 --> 07:19.790
You can have this back.

07:19.790 --> 07:21.120
It doesn't fit.

07:22.210 --> 07:23.130
Sure.

07:24.590 --> 07:27.460
And after all I've done for you!

07:27.460 --> 07:29.090
Life is cruel!

07:32.090 --> 07:35.500
She has another friend besides Yuma...

07:36.010 --> 07:41.190
There's so much I still don't know about Matoi.

07:45.270 --> 07:46.570
Clarus-san?

07:46.570 --> 07:47.610
What?

07:47.610 --> 07:52.150
I'm happy you're protecting me, and I'm really grateful...

07:52.150 --> 07:54.820
But can't you dress more normally, so you don't stand out?

07:55.120 --> 07:56.740
I can't.

07:57.490 --> 08:01.580
The clothes Fatima provided me with are all that I own.

08:03.030 --> 08:05.170
So you don't dress up?

08:05.170 --> 08:06.000
Dress up?

08:07.340 --> 08:09.130
I guess you don't think about that stuff.

08:09.130 --> 08:11.300
What a waste. You're too cute not to.

08:13.260 --> 08:14.180
Oh yeah, we can do that!

08:15.970 --> 08:17.900
Okay, goodnight!

08:18.350 --> 08:19.600
What was that about?

08:22.560 --> 08:22.600
Tasty Water Born from the Mountains

08:22.560 --> 08:22.600
Summer Leisure Outings Specials

08:22.560 --> 08:22.600
Mountains・Beaches・Lakes

08:22.560 --> 08:22.600
Day Hikes
on mountains
recommended
for beginners

08:22.560 --> 08:22.600
Enjoy camping
like a real man!

08:22.600 --> 08:22.640
Tasty Water Born from the Mountains

08:22.600 --> 08:22.640
Summer Leisure Outings Specials

08:22.600 --> 08:22.640
Mountains・Beaches・Lakes

08:22.940 --> 08:25.270
You're on a train bound for Tokyo?

08:26.560 --> 08:28.860
What's the meaning of this, Clarus?

08:28.860 --> 08:30.360
I don't know.

08:30.360 --> 08:32.450
She wouldn't give me a reason when I asked.

08:33.490 --> 08:35.000
Continue your guard duties.

08:35.490 --> 08:37.870
Don't let her out of your sight.

08:37.870 --> 08:39.290
Understood.

08:42.000 --> 08:43.960
Harajuku Station

08:49.380 --> 08:49.420
The cutest place ever! Welcome to Harajuku!

08:50.920 --> 08:50.960
T-Shirts
w/ Logos

08:50.960 --> 08:51.010
Hot
drinks!

08:50.960 --> 08:51.010
Cute Photo Booths!

09:03.480 --> 09:04.940
What is this place?

09:04.940 --> 09:07.400
A place where you can find the cutest things...

09:07.400 --> 09:10.020
...in all of Japan!

09:10.900 --> 09:12.190
I don't understand.

09:12.190 --> 09:13.900
Anyway, let's go!

09:13.900 --> 09:15.150
Go where?

09:15.990 --> 09:16.740
Ah, wait—

09:17.570 --> 09:19.200
Shopping, of course!

10:30.600 --> 10:32.190
X X

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Kiwi Creme

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Banana Custard

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Strawberry Cheesecake

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Whip Cream

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Mango

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Gelato Caramel Cheesecake

10:32.190 --> 10:32.230
Gelato Apple Cinnamon

10:35.110 --> 10:35.150
Gelato Apple Cinnamon

10:53.170 --> 10:53.210
Super-Sized
Portions

11:01.930 --> 11:05.100
We got excited and ate too much.

11:07.980 --> 11:09.060
Hey.

11:09.060 --> 11:12.100
You're spending so much on clothes and food for me.

11:12.100 --> 11:13.610
I can't pay you back.

11:13.610 --> 11:15.270
It's fine.

11:15.270 --> 11:17.990
I'm doing this because I want to.

11:17.990 --> 11:19.860
You must have a strange idea of normal.

11:20.280 --> 11:22.110
Really?

11:22.110 --> 11:23.370
Okay!

11:23.370 --> 11:26.100
I want you to pay me back!

11:26.100 --> 11:29.460
It's something only you can do.

11:29.460 --> 11:31.120
Will you do it for me?

11:31.120 --> 11:32.580
If I can, I will.

11:34.210 --> 11:35.460
Yay!

11:35.460 --> 11:36.920
Yay! Yay!

11:36.920 --> 11:39.670
<i>I have a really bad feeling about this.</i>

11:44.140 --> 11:47.060
Even though my ancestors were exorcists,

11:47.060 --> 11:48.950
no matter how many times I repeat the ritual dance,

11:48.950 --> 11:51.350
a god never comes down to me!

11:51.350 --> 11:53.560
But I'm sure I'm capable!

11:53.560 --> 11:57.650
I can even see the demons
when normal people can't.

11:57.650 --> 12:02.360
I thought you might have some answers.

12:02.740 --> 12:05.370
<i>Oh. So </i>this<i> is what she was planning.</i>

12:05.780 --> 12:07.620
Tell it to me straight, Clarus-san.

12:07.620 --> 12:10.580
Will a god ever come down to me?

12:10.580 --> 12:11.870
I don't know.

12:11.870 --> 12:14.540
No, don't say that!

12:14.790 --> 12:19.710
However, I can test whether or not you are capable of achieving Divine Union.

12:20.710 --> 12:23.010
There's the words I was lookin' for!

12:23.970 --> 12:26.090
<i>But I was having so much fun shopping!</i>

12:26.720 --> 12:29.180
The test is simple.

12:30.390 --> 12:34.940
There is a being from a higher dimension sealed inside this box, and I can release it temporarily.

12:34.940 --> 12:37.060
Then I can see how you well you align with it.

12:37.360 --> 12:39.270
This isn't dangerous, is it?

12:39.270 --> 12:43.240
Don't worry. A light test won't hurt her.

12:43.240 --> 12:45.200
Sounds good to me! Let her rip!

12:45.530 --> 12:46.320
Of course.

12:47.870 --> 12:50.700
System halt. Status: unconfined.

13:05.300 --> 13:07.550
This is Clarus-san's god...

13:07.930 --> 13:08.550
Let's begin.

13:12.390 --> 13:13.930
She repelled it?

13:13.930 --> 13:16.800
It should have passed through her if she didn't align with it.

13:17.310 --> 13:18.200
Why?

13:19.190 --> 13:21.360
Clarus-san! Hit me again!

13:21.360 --> 13:23.360
Yuma-chan, that's enough!

13:23.360 --> 13:24.490
No!

13:24.490 --> 13:25.360
What are you—

13:25.360 --> 13:28.160
I want a god too!

13:28.160 --> 13:28.990
The output's—

13:32.160 --> 13:33.620
Right here!

13:39.580 --> 13:41.090
Yuma-chan!

13:41.090 --> 13:42.380
I'm not done yet!

13:43.500 --> 13:45.090
I...

13:54.270 --> 13:55.980
Wh-What's going on?

13:55.980 --> 13:57.440
Yuma-chan!

13:58.350 --> 14:00.190
M-Master Seigen!?

14:01.190 --> 14:02.900
The jewel of sealing is...

14:02.900 --> 14:05.610
If this jewel has split,

14:05.610 --> 14:09.700
that means the barrier I put in place has been opened.

14:09.700 --> 14:10.820
Yuma.

14:20.880 --> 14:25.000
A-A tanuki and a fox came out of you!

14:25.000 --> 14:26.530
Higher dimensional beings?

14:27.330 --> 14:29.740
These are my gods?

14:31.680 --> 14:34.180
Yay! I did it!

14:34.180 --> 14:35.930
Or rather, I'd already done it!

14:35.930 --> 14:39.000
I've been an exorcist girl all along!

14:39.000 --> 14:42.060
She was aligned with a
higher dimensional being already?

14:42.060 --> 14:43.230
So that's why mine was repelled.

14:43.820 --> 14:48.440
Hi, Tanuki-san and Fox-san. I'm Yuma!

14:49.490 --> 14:51.280
They transformed!

14:51.570 --> 14:52.780
What does that mean?

14:52.780 --> 14:54.410
I don't know.

14:54.410 --> 14:57.410
You two are so cute!

15:02.210 --> 15:04.340
The three of us will—

15:04.340 --> 15:07.380
Huh? Wh-Where are you going?

15:11.880 --> 15:13.340
What's going on?

15:13.340 --> 15:15.260
Judging from the situation,

15:15.260 --> 15:20.060
they were aligned with her already,
but have never been released until now.

15:20.730 --> 15:24.400
It is likely that there was some sort of seal,

15:24.400 --> 15:27.320
and my test broke it.

15:27.860 --> 15:29.030
We need to chase them down quickly.

15:30.190 --> 15:33.950
There's no telling what beings that
have been sealed for ages might do.

15:40.410 --> 15:42.120
People are panicking.

15:42.120 --> 15:44.580
Of course they are. Most people can't see them.

15:44.920 --> 15:47.040
We need to catch them already!

15:47.040 --> 15:49.210
We'll have to get ahead of them first.

15:49.210 --> 15:50.460
How?

15:50.460 --> 15:52.550
Divine Union. How else?

15:52.550 --> 15:54.320
What? <i>Here</i>?

15:57.510 --> 15:59.350
Please, Toi-san!

15:59.350 --> 16:00.810
You're right!

16:02.810 --> 16:04.560
We have no choice.

16:04.560 --> 16:07.520
System halt. Status: unconfined.

16:07.770 --> 16:08.940
Divine Union!

16:21.120 --> 16:24.170
I'll travel through the higher dimensions so we don't stand out.

16:24.170 --> 16:24.830
Follow me.

16:24.830 --> 16:26.000
O-Okay!

16:26.000 --> 16:27.880
Take me, too!

16:27.880 --> 16:28.840
No.

16:28.840 --> 16:32.220
If they see you again, they'll turn and run.

16:32.550 --> 16:34.510
But...

16:34.510 --> 16:35.970
Wait for us, Yuma-chan.

16:35.970 --> 16:38.300
I promise we'll bring them back.

16:41.930 --> 16:44.600
I can't just stay put!

16:44.600 --> 16:47.400
I'm gonna look for my gods too!

16:50.610 --> 16:53.810
Harajuku Station

16:50.980 --> 16:53.240
It looked like they were headed this way.

16:53.820 --> 16:54.950
Who are those girls?

16:54.950 --> 16:56.700
Are they filming a TV show or something?

16:56.700 --> 16:57.780
I know her.

16:57.780 --> 16:59.830
It's that "Exorcist Girl" that's all over the Internet!

16:58.200 --> 17:01.490
Clarus, we're still standing out...

17:05.210 --> 17:06.870
I found them! This way!

17:06.870 --> 17:08.290
Hey, wait—

17:12.960 --> 17:15.260
Fox-san, Tanuki-san...

17:15.260 --> 17:16.800
Where are you?

17:21.350 --> 17:22.810
I've lost sight of them.

17:22.810 --> 17:25.770
If they hid in the forest,
tracking them down will be difficult.

17:25.770 --> 17:26.940
Oh, that's right!

17:27.270 --> 17:29.310
I have an idea.

17:33.820 --> 17:34.820
What's that?

17:34.820 --> 17:37.400
Foxes love fried tofu!

17:37.400 --> 17:39.280
We'll draw them out with it!

17:39.280 --> 17:40.570
Okay...

17:41.330 --> 17:43.540
Do you really think higher-dimensional beings will be fooled by—

17:45.580 --> 17:46.500
Here they come!

17:50.630 --> 17:52.200
And she's a little glutton to boot!

17:52.200 --> 17:53.600
Now, Clarus-san!

17:53.600 --> 17:54.500
Right!

17:54.710 --> 17:56.670
Gotcha—

17:57.090 --> 17:57.930
Huh?

18:00.590 --> 18:02.310
Stuffed animals?

18:02.310 --> 18:03.310
They made decoys!?

18:03.310 --> 18:04.680
Then where did the real ones go!?

18:04.680 --> 18:06.810
There she is! The Exorcist Girl!

18:06.810 --> 18:08.590
Is she going to purify demons?

18:08.590 --> 18:11.270
Let me get a video!

18:08.590 --> 18:11.270
D-Don't take my picture! Don't post this...

18:11.270 --> 18:13.730
Um... um...

18:12.190 --> 18:15.230
<i>Y-Yuma-chan, sorry!</i>

18:16.940 --> 18:19.320
Fox-san, Tanuki-san...

18:19.320 --> 18:21.200
Where are you?

18:21.200 --> 18:23.530
I... I...

18:27.460 --> 18:30.000
Why? Why?

18:39.880 --> 18:45.600
Please, let me see Fox-san and Tanuki-san.

18:45.600 --> 18:46.520
Please.

18:56.110 --> 19:00.490
Let me see Fox-san and Tanuki-san.

19:00.490 --> 19:01.990
Please.

19:21.270 --> 19:26.720
I guess they hate me, don't they?

19:26.720 --> 19:29.850
Enough to run away from me at first sight.

19:35.270 --> 19:38.030
But even if they hate me,

19:38.030 --> 19:44.370
I'm happy I got to meet them.

19:58.170 --> 20:00.610
Fox-san! Tanuki-san!

20:00.610 --> 20:02.200
Let's play together!

20:18.410 --> 20:20.360
That's my granddaughter!

20:20.360 --> 20:21.860
Attagirl!

20:21.860 --> 20:25.490
But it's too soon for this!

20:27.240 --> 20:30.040
<i>Stay in this dimension.</i>

20:36.950 --> 20:36.990
Entrance
.Ceremony

20:52.310 --> 20:53.600
I...

21:05.200 --> 21:07.800
Fox-san! Tanuki-san!

21:12.370 --> 21:15.830
want to be with you.

21:17.120 --> 21:19.040
Will you stay with me?

21:50.280 --> 21:52.740
I'm going to dance too!

22:00.790 --> 22:02.170
I'm glad...

22:02.170 --> 22:02.880
Indeed.

22:06.510 --> 22:07.630
Wow.

22:07.630 --> 22:10.340
I didn't know you could
smile like that, Clarus-san.

22:10.680 --> 22:11.800
Cute.

22:12.430 --> 22:16.640
H-Her dance was just so weird... a-and I thought it was funny!

22:17.310 --> 22:20.150
Sure. Whatever you say.

22:20.150 --> 22:21.230
Cheeky, aren't you?

22:26.660 --> 22:28.820
Feeling your heart

22:28.820 --> 22:37.580
hito wa umarenagara hikari to kage wo

22:28.820 --> 22:37.580
It's natural for us all to be followed

22:37.580 --> 22:43.590
matoi tsuzukeru

22:37.580 --> 22:43.590
by light and shadow

22:43.590 --> 22:47.090
The lonely one

22:49.260 --> 22:51.300
Feeling your heart

22:51.300 --> 23:00.020
You can obtain all you've ever wanted

22:51.350 --> 23:00.060
hoshii mono subete te ni ireru koto

23:00.020 --> 23:06.280
sore ga shiawase nano

23:00.020 --> 23:06.280
But is that truly happiness?

23:06.280 --> 23:11.240
darekaga egao nara

23:06.280 --> 23:11.240
If someone is smiling,

23:11.240 --> 23:17.750
dokokade kitto naiteru hito ga ite

23:11.240 --> 23:17.750
somewhere, someone else is probably crying

23:17.750 --> 23:23.960
surechigau hodo itooshiku omou

23:17.750 --> 23:23.960
As our paths continue to cross,

23:23.960 --> 23:28.760
kimochi ga aru

23:23.960 --> 23:28.760
our love grows stronger

23:28.760 --> 23:33.760
hitotoki no aida ni

23:28.760 --> 23:33.760
In that short span of time

23:33.760 --> 23:40.270
bokura wa minna mujun wo dakishimete

23:33.760 --> 23:40.270
we embrace all contradictions

23:40.270 --> 23:48.400
as we watch the lights that lead us to tomorrow

23:40.310 --> 23:48.450
ashita e no hikari wo mitsume nagara

23:48.400 --> 23:53.580
aruiteku no kana

23:48.400 --> 23:53.580
I wonder if we'll keep walking this path

23:57.330 --> 24:00.080
I have an announcement, everyone!

24:00.080 --> 24:03.210
Starting next week, this ain't
"Matoi the Sacred Slayer" any longer,

